mmodities, particularly food, were prevalent from the very beginning and became ever more acute during the German occupation. Meanwhile, German efforts to strictly control the consumption of food and other basic goods in Warsaw led to widespread smuggling and thriving black markets, which advantaged those who could pay even higher prices in order to access vital resources.<\/p>","DOI":"10.7591\/cornell\/9781501705236.003.0003","type":"book-chapter","created":{"date-parts":[[2017,12,18]],"date-time":"2017-12-18T16:05:46Z","timestamp":1513613146000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Living on the Edge"],"prefix":"10.7591","author":[{"given":"Robert","family":"Blobaum","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"4434","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2017,9,21]]},"container-title":["A Minor Apocalypse"],"original-title":["Living on the Edge"],"language":"en","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2022,7,28]],"date-time":"2022-07-28T18:58:35Z","timestamp":1659034715000},"score":20.339134,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/academic.oup.com\/cornell-scholarship-online\/book\/19032\/chapter\/177417902"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2017,2,1]]},"ISBN":["9781501705236","9781501707889"],"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.7591\/cornell\/9781501705236.003.0003","published":{"date-parts":[[2017,2,1]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2022,7,7]],"date-time":"2022-07-07T11:14:41Z","timestamp":1657192481725},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Oxford University Press","isbn-type":[{"value":"9780198847281","type":"print"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1894,1,1]]},"DOI":"10.1093\/actrade\/9780198847281.book.1","type":"book","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,4,28]],"date-time":"2020-04-28T13:17:55Z","timestamp":1588079875000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["The Complete Works of Geoffrey Chaucer, Vol. 1: Romaunt of the Ro